# build-image: the host's pacman.conf ships inside the public image — evidence
# Card t_b7457840, 2026-11-17.
#
# Build host: a throwaway archlinux:latest container (the CI image) whose /etc/pacman.conf was
# given a sentinel repository, [leak] (an empty but loadable file:// repo), to stand in for
# whatever repositories a build host may have configured. Image: emunix-2026.11.30-x86_64.img,
# built with EMUNIX_REPO_URL=file:///work/out/repo, the local signed [emunix] repository.
#
# Sections 1-2 are the exit criterion; 3 runs the same check against the image built before this
# change, to show it catches the leak that actually shipped.
==================================================================
1. The build
==================================================================
Created symlink '/etc/systemd/system/default.target' → '/usr/lib/systemd/system/multi-user.target'.
Built /work/out/emunix-2026.11.30-x86_64.img (24G apparent, 3.0G on disk)
Version 2026.11.30, snapshot latest, device none

==================================================================
2. The exit criterion
==================================================================
## The build host: /etc/pacman.conf carries a repository the image must not ship
$ grep -c "^\[leak\]" /etc/pacman.conf
1
$ grep -n -A2 "^\[leak\]" /etc/pacman.conf
108:[leak]
109-SigLevel = Never
110-Server = file:///srv/leak

## The gate
$ bash build/verify-image.sh /work/out/emunix-2026.11.30-x86_64.img
verified /work/out/emunix-2026.11.30-x86_64.img: 5 labels, systemd-boot + 2 entries, kernel/initramfs, fstab + mounts, retrogamer, machine-id

## Inside rootfs_a: the sentinel is gone
$ grep -c '^\[leak\]' <rootfs_a>/etc/pacman.conf
0
$ grep -o "^\[[^]]*\]" <rootfs_a>/etc/pacman.conf
[options]
[core]
[extra]
[emunix]

## The file that ships in the image: <rootfs_a>/etc/pacman.conf
# Written by build/build-image.sh, not taken from the build host. The official repositories the
# image installs from; [emunix] is appended during the build.
[options]
HoldPkg     = pacman glibc
Architecture = auto
CacheDir    = /var/cache/pacman/pkg/
SigLevel    = Required DatabaseOptional
LocalFileSigLevel = Optional

[core]
Include = /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist

[extra]
Include = /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist

[emunix]
Server = file:///var/cache/emunix-repo
SigLevel = Required DatabaseRequired

## The four [emunix] packages still resolve there, in the image chroot
$ pacman -S --print-format %r emunix-keyring -> emunix
$ pacman -S --print-format %r ryzenadj -> emunix
$ pacman -S --print-format %r freeimage -> emunix
$ pacman -S --print-format %r emulationstation-de -> emunix
$ pacman -Sl leak   (the host repository is not configured in the image)
error: repository "leak" was not found.
(no such repository: expected)

==================================================================
3. The new check against the image built before this change
==================================================================
$ bash build/verify-image.sh /work/out/emunix-2026.11.20-x86_64.img
FAIL: pacman.conf carries what the image template does not: [options] NoProgressBar
[options] VerbosePkgLists
[options] ParallelDownloads
[options] DownloadUser
[options] DisableSandboxFilesystem
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
[options] NoExtract
exit=1

# What this does not prove
#
# - That a *release* is built this way. The Release pipeline runs the same build and verify steps
#   on a tag; it is proven here only in a local container, and the GitHub Release path itself is
#   not exercised (publishing is BP's one-way door).
# - That no other build-host state leaks into the image. This card closes build-host pacman.conf
#   only. /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist still comes from the host (pacstrap copies it by design), so a
#   host's mirror list does ship; it carries no credentials, and replacing it is a separate card.
# - That CI's own container is clean. It is the same archlinux:latest image as here, whose
#   /etc/pacman.conf carries the docker options this card now keeps out of the image; the check
#   in section 3 shows those options are rejected if they arrive.
# - The [emunix] Server in this image is file:///var/cache/emunix-repo, because the build used
#   EMUNIX_REPO_URL=file:// for a local repository. A CI/release build writes the Pages URL.
